---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Accessibility statement for the Village of Midvale website."
  eyebrow="Accessibility"
  intro="Our commitment to making this site usable by everyone."
>
  <h2>Conformance</h2>
  <p>
    The Village of Midvale website is designed to conform to
    <strong>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 Level AA</strong>,
    with Level AAA where reasonable &mdash; particularly color contrast.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is also intended to satisfy the requirements of
    Section 508 of the Rehabilitation Act and to meet the de facto expectations
    of the Americans with Disabilities Act for state and local government
    digital services.
  </p>

  <h2>What we've done</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Visible focus indicators on every interactive element.</li>
    <li>A "Skip to main content" link as the first focusable element on every page.</li>
    <li>Heading levels in correct order, with one <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> per page.</li>
    <li>Form inputs always have visible labels and clear error messages.</li>
    <li>All non-decorative images include meaningful <code>alt</code> text.</li>
    <li>Color is never the only means of conveying information.</li>
    <li>Keyboard-only navigation works on every page.</li>
    <li>Semantic HTML throughout; ARIA used sparingly and only where semantic HTML can't.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Found a problem?</h2>
  <p>
    If you encounter an accessibility barrier on this site, please let us know
    so we can fix it. The fastest way is the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>;
    you can also call the village office at the number on the contact page.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you need a public document in an alternate format (large print, plain text,
    audio), include the request in your message and we will respond with the
    document or with an estimated timeline.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
